{"title":"Vega Logistics","sub":"Solar on the warehouse roof: buy the panels or buy the power?","type":"Investment / capacity","industry":"Energy","geo":"United States","diff":2,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"NPV · own vs lease · energy economics","prompt":"Vega runs a large distribution warehouse in Arizona. It can put solar panels on the roof for $1.5M, or let a solar developer install them for free and buy the power under a 25-year contract (a power purchase agreement, PPA). The CFO asks which is better, using Vega's 8% cost of capital.","clarify":[{"q":"Output?","a":"About 1,800 MWh a year for 25 years."},{"q":"How much would Vega use itself?","a":"About 70%; the rest would be exported to the grid when the warehouse is quiet."},{"q":"Prices?","a":"Vega pays $120 per MWh for grid power. Exported power earns $40 per MWh. Maintenance costs about $20k a year if Vega owns the panels."},{"q":"PPA?","a":"The developer would sell Vega the power it uses at $90 per MWh, and keep any exports."}],"structure":{"root":"Should Vega own the panels or sign a PPA?","branches":[{"head":"Owning","items":["Upfront cost","Yearly savings and export income","Maintenance","NPV over 25 years"]},{"head":"PPA","items":["Saving vs grid price","No upfront cost"]},{"head":"Other factors","items":["Use of capital","Risk of the roof or the business changing"]}]},"hypothesis":"Owning gives the full saving but ties up capital; a PPA gives a smaller saving with no investment. At an 8% cost of capital, the PPA could well win.","questions":[{"q":"What is owning worth, in NPV and payback?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Yearly benefit: 1,800 × (70% × $120 + 30% × $40) − $20k = <b>$152.8k</b>.</p> <p>25 years at 8% discount factor: 10.67. NPV = −$1,500k + $152.8k × 10.67 = <b>$131k</b>. Payback: 9.8 years.</p>","note":"Present value of $1 a year for 25 years at 8% = 10.67."},{"q":"What is the PPA worth?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"400.493pt\" height=\"174.352pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 400.493 174.352\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 174.352 L 400.493 174.352 L 400.493 0 L 0 0 L 0 174.352 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 47.333 138.336 L 393.293 138.336 L 393.293 10.824 L 47.333 10.824 L 47.333 138.336 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"mff7d576334\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#mff7d576334\" x=\"107.988325\" y=\"138.336\" style=\"fill: #555555; stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #555555\" transform=\"translate(75.654418 154.03) scale(0.09 -0.09)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-22\" d=\"M 2445 -64 Q 1818 -64 1360 217 Q 902 499 659 1040 Q 416 1581 416 2355 Q 416 3136 665 3686 Q 915 4237 1369 4525 Q 1824 4813 2451 4813 Q 3078 4813 3529 4525 Q 3981 4237 4227 3693 Q 4474 3149 4474 2362 Q 4474 1587 4230 1046 Q 3987 506 3529 221 Q 3072 -64 2445 -64 L 2445 -64 z\nM 2458 403 Q 3149 403 3491 880 Q 3834 1357 3834 2355 Q 3834 3373 3485 3859 Q 3136 4346 2451 4346 Q 1760 4346 1408 3856 Q 1056 3366 1056 2355 Q 1056 1363 1408 883 Q 1760 403 2458 403 L 2458 403 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-73\" d=\"M 4832 3392 Q 4870 3392 4889 3363 Q 4909 3334 4896 3296 L 3917 83 Q 3904 38 3875 19 Q 3846 0 3795 0 L 3488 0 Q 3379 0 3354 83 L 2592 2477 Q 2566 2534 2547 2534 Q 2528 2534 2515 2477 L 1792 83 Q 1779 38 1750 19 Q 1722 0 1670 0 L 1344 0 Q 1242 0 1210 83 L 198 3296 Q 192 3334 211 3363 Q 230 3392 275 3392 L 653 3392 Q 691 3392 716 3376 Q 742 3360 755 3322 L 1517 832 Q 1536 768 1561 771 Q 1587 774 1613 838 L 2368 3328 Q 2381 3360 2403 3376 Q 2426 3392 2458 3392 L 2758 339