 miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"text_10\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(101.704575 96.990178) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-83\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(110.59375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_11\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(212.70925 27.55295) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" d=\"M 2362 4806 Q 2605 4806 2797 4755 Q 2989 4704 3142 4614 Q 3296 4525 3414 4416 Q 3533 4307 3610 4186 Q 3622 4160 3625 4131 Q 3629 4102 3590 4083 L 3226 3936 Q 3194 3917 3168 3933 Q 3142 3949 3130 3974 Q 2989 4141 2813 4243 Q 2637 4346 2368 4346 Q 1907 4346 1609 4122 Q 1312 3898 1171 3510 Q 1030 3123 1030 2637 Q 1030 2534 1049 2502 Q 1069 2470 1146 2509 Q 1389 2630 1670 2732 Q 1952 2835 2330 2835 Q 2822 2835 3171 2652 Q 3520 2470 3702 2156 Q 3885 1843 3885 1446 Q 3885 998 3664 656 Q 3443 314 3068 128 Q 2694 -58 2234 -58 Q 1670 -58 1264 220 Q 858 499 640 1027 Q 422 1555 422 2304 Q 422 3085 656 3645 Q 890 4205 1325 4505 Q 1760 4806 2362 4806 L 2362 4806 z\nM 2259 2387 Q 2093 2387 1885 2345 Q 1677 2304 1491 2240 Q 1306 2176 1171 2093 Q 1094 2042 1068 1987 Q 1043 1933 1043 1818 Q 1043 1587 1116 1340 Q 1190 1094 1334 876 Q 1478 659 1702 524 Q 1926 390 2234 390 Q 2534 390 2768 524 Q 3002 659 3139 896 Q 3277 1133 3277 1421 Q 3277 1690 3155 1910 Q 3034 2131 2803 2259 Q 2573 2387 2259 2387 L 2259 2387 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-83\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" transform=\"translate(64.09375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-82\" transform=\"translate(130.1875 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_12\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(324.6933 14.928) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(64.90625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" transform=\"translate(133.703125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pb9d237e5ab\"><rect x=\"47.333\" y=\"10.824\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · NPV at 8% ($k)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Vega saves $120 − $90 = $30 on each MWh it uses: 1,800 × 70% × $30 = $37.8k a year, with no investment.</p> <p>NPV: $37.8k × 10.67 = <b>$404k</b>, about 3× the NPV of owning.</p>"},{"q":"Owning only just pays. Why, and what could change that?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Thirty percent of the power is exported at $40, a third of the grid price, and Vega's 8% cost of capital is high for a 25-year asset. If Vega charged its electric forklifts in daytime and used 85% on site, owning would be worth $362k, still below the PPA.</p> <p>The developer can own panels more cheaply because its cost of capital is lower. Vega's capital is better spent on its core business.</p>"}],"reco":"Sign the PPA. Owning the panels has an NPV of only about $131k at Vega's 8% cost of capital, because 30% of the power is exported cheaply, while the PPA saves about $38k a year with no investment, an NPV of about $404k. Even using 85% of the power on site, owning stays behind. Negotiate the PPA price, a price-escalation cap and what happens if Vega leaves the building. Next step: get two more developer quotes.","great":["Values both options with the same discount rate and life","Values export and self-used power differently","Sees how cost of capital favours the PPA","Checks whether more self-use changes the answer"],"id":83,"slug":"vega-logistics"}